{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-MRSA, Synergistic AMPs, Antibiofilm, Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Discovery: isolated from spider venom via HPLC. Whole sequence was then obtained by comparing the detected sequence with the transcriptome data. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is 44% similar to Meucin-24 K: 24%. GRAVY: -0.876; mol Wt: 3088.76; mol formula: C140H235N39O35S2; mol ex coeff: 1490. Chemical modification: C-terminal amidation. Activity: active against Gram- S. typhimurium CGMCC 1.1174 (MIC 2.5 uM), E. coli CCTCC AB 2018675 (MIC 5 uM), S. dysenteriae CGMCC 1.1869 (MIC 2.5 uM), P. aeruginosa CGMCC 1.596 (MIC 5-10 uM), K. pneumoniae (MIC 10 uM), A. baumannii (MIC 5-10 uM), Gram+ S. aureus CMCC 26003 or MRSA ATCC 43300 (MIC 5 uM), and E. faecium (MIC 2.5 uM). Bacterial killing effect. Antibiofilm:bacteria: inhibited bacterial biofilm formation:E. coli and inhibited bacterial biofilm formation:S. aureus; disrupted bacterial biofilm:E. coli and disrupted bacterial biofilm:S. aureus (24 h). Resistance development:no:bacteria:E. coli: Both E. coli and Resistance development:no:bacteria:S. aureus did not develop resistance to this peptide after 21 passages. MOA:bacteria:E. coli: MOA:bacteria:S. aureus: permeated bacterial membranes by forming pores. Structure: largely random coil in water and helical in TFE (50%). Peptide stability: heat-stable after exposure at 80oC or 100oC for 1 h. Antimicrobial robustness: NaCl-insensitive:E. coli (150 mM), KCl-insensitive:E. coli (4.5 mM), NH4Cl-insensitive:E. coli (6 uM), MgCl2-insensitive:E. coli (1 mM), CaCl2-sensitive:E. coli (2.5 mM); NaCl-insensitive:S. aureus (150 mM), KCl-insensitive:S. aureus (4.5 mM), NH4Cl-insensitive:S. aureus (6 uM), MgCl2-insensitive:S. aureus (1 mM), CaCl2-insensitive:S. aureus (2.5 mM). In vitro toxicity: 10.13% hemolysis at 320 uM: poorly hemo.lytic. Low toxicity to normal cells LO2, HEK293T, cancer cells HepG2, and HONE-1, but toxic to mouse breast cancer cells 4T1 (IC50 20 uM). In vivo toxicity:mouse:IM: No death or notable toxic effects were observed. Animal model:mouse: netropenic mice thigh infection model, treated 2 h post-infection, reduced CFU by 1.35 log after 48 h (i.m./i.m.). Synergy:antibiotics:levofloxacin: only showed synergistic killing with levofloxacin against S. aureus (FICI 0.31). Est.12/2024; updated 4/2025", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39620694", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Antimicrob Agents Chemother. 2025 Jan 31;69(1):e0042424. doi: 10.1128/aac.00424-24. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP05069", "source_id": "AP05069", "source_numeric_id": "05069", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP05069", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "LC-AMP-I1, a novel venom-derived antimicrobial peptide from the wolf spider Lycosa coelestis.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
